BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:What We Inherit\, What We Create\; Collage as Reflection
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T160000
UID:a57cfef4459ed325d7c9e696db4e38f1@petalumaartscenter.org
DESCRIPTION:In dialogue with our upcoming The Threads That Connect Us exhi
 bition\, this workshop uses found imagery\, vintage ephemera\, and contemp
 orary materials to reflect on memory\, place\, and the textures of everyda
 y life. Participants will create layered works that balance personal narra
 tive with broader cultural reference. Emphasis will be placed on editing\,
  composition\, and allowing materials to suggest meaning rather than worki
 ng toward a fixed outcome. All experience levels are welcome. Instructors 
 : Robin Borelli \, Laura Engdahl \, and Jen Siddens (Click their names to 
 view their links) May 16\, 2026 12:00pm – 4:00pm $150 Members\, $170 Non
 -Members Materials : Two 12” x 12” wood panels and heavy art paper&nbs
 p\;are provided and included in the price.&nbsp\; A supply list of other a
 rt supplies for participants to bring will be provided upon registration.&
 nbsp\;Participants are also encouraged to bring copies of personal photogr
 aphs\, letters\, maps\, or printed matter that feel connected to their own
  sense of personal history\, though some shared collage materials will als
 o be provided. #block-7a14000312225e29e91d { } #block-7a14000312225e29e91d
